{
  "name": "pol_waveplate_oblique",
  "description": "The axis of a part as the ray sees it, theta_eff = atan2(sin theta (d . n), cos theta) (contract v2 \u00a74.5: an absorbing polarizer passes d x a, a positive uniaxial plate's fast wave is along d x c), anchor 'projection'. Half-wave plates with the fast axis at 30 deg in their own frame on horizontal light: HWP1 hit at 40 deg incidence sees 23.858655 deg and gives linear 47.717310 deg; HWP2 hit from behind sees -30 (= 150) deg and gives 120 deg (s = [-0.5, -0.866025, 0]); HWP3 from the front at normal incidence sees 30 and gives 60 deg (s = [-0.5, 0.866025, 0]). Unpolarized light through polarizer P4 (axis 30 deg, 40 deg incidence) leaves linear along the axis it sees, 23.858655 deg, p = 0.5.",
